# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository and in working copies.
#
# Development happens on Windows but the application runs in Alpine containers.
# Without this, Git rewrites checkouts to CRLF, which fights Prettier's
# `endOfLine: lf` and produces whole-file diffs that hide the real change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts MUST be LF — a CRLF shebang fails inside a container with an
# unhelpful "no such file or directory".
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PARSER FIXTURES ARE BYTE-EXACT. Do not let Git touch their line endings.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` above would rewrite the CRLF fixtures to LF, which would:
#   · make `boa-*-crlf.csv` byte-identical to its LF twin, so the fixture proving
#     the parser handles CRLF would silently stop proving anything, and
#   · change every recorded digest in tests/unit/fixture-guard.test.ts, so a fresh
#     clone would fail the checksum test for a reason that looks like a bug.
#
# These files are INPUT DATA, not source. Their bytes — line endings, the BOM, the
# fixed-width padding, the trailing spaces — are exactly what is under test.
# Caught by `git add` warning that CRLF "will be replaced by LF".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tests/fixtures/** -text

# Generated; keep diffs collapsed in reviews.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true
drizzle/**/*.sql linguist-generated=true
drizzle/meta/** linguist-generated=true

# Binary.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
